From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm630: let modem own pipe filters

The downstream SDM630/660 IPA node declares
qcom,modem-cfg-emb-pipe-flt.  On these platforms Q6/uC programs the
embedded filtering table for APPS_LAN_WAN_PROD.  The AP driver must not
replace that pipe's filter pointer with a separately allocated table.

Describe the same hardware ownership in the mainline device tree.  The
ipa2-lite QMI path already honours this property: it accepts the modem's
rules and enables filtering without installing or reapplying an AP-owned
pipe-4 table.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
index 564bbb0..b459390 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
@@ -1040,5 +1040,6 @@
 		ipa: ipa@14780000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,ipa-lite-v2.6";
+			qcom,modem-cfg-emb-pipe-flt;
 			reg = <0x14780000 0x47000>;
 			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_IPA_CLK>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 333 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
-- 
